## 3. Architecture & Design

### 3.1 Design Principles

#### 3.1.1 Single Responsibility
Each method handles one specific task:
- `_read_file()`: File I/O operations only
- `_extract_data_from_sheet()`: Data slicing only
- `_save_output_file()`: File writing only

#### 3.1.2 Configuration Over Code
All operational parameters externalized:
- Folder paths
- Sheet specifications
- Column/row ranges
- Header handling
- Post-processing actions

#### 3.1.3 Fail-Safe Operation
- Graceful degradation on errors
- Partial success handling (process available sheets)
- No data corruption on failure
- Comprehensive error logging

#### 3.1.4 Data Integrity First
- Read-only mode for input files
- String-based data handling (no type coercion)
- Atomic file operations
- Verification logging

### 3.2 Class Structure

```python
DataExtractor
├── __init__()                          # Initialize logging
├── _setup_logging()                    # Configure log handlers
├── _validate_folders()                 # Pre-flight checks
├── _detect_new_file()                  # File system monitoring
├── _read_file(path, has_header)        # File ingestion
├── _convert_column_letter_to_index()   # Column mapping
├── _extract_data_from_sheet(df, config)# Data slicing
├── _generate_output_filename()         # Naming logic
├── _save_output_file(df, path, fmt)    # File writing
├── _process_file(path)                 # Orchestration
├── _move_processed_file(path)          # Post-processing
└── run()                               # Main loop
```

