## 7. Technical Specifications

### 7.1 File Format Support

#### 7.1.1 Supported Input Formats
| Format | Extension | Engine | Notes |
|--------|-----------|--------|-------|
| Excel 2007+ | .xlsx | openpyxl | Full support, recommended |
| Excel 97-2003 | .xls | xlrd | Limited support, legacy |
| Excel Macro | .xlsm | openpyxl | Macros ignored, data extracted |
| CSV | .csv | pandas | UTF-8 encoding assumed |

#### 7.1.2 Supported Output Formats
| Format | Extension | Use Case |
|--------|-----------|----------|
| CSV | .csv | Universal compatibility, smaller size |
| Excel | .xlsx | Excel integration, formatting preserved |

### 7.2 Data Type Handling

#### 7.2.1 String-Based Processing
All data is read and processed as strings (`dtype=str`):
- **Benefit**: Preserves exact representation from source
- **Impact**: No automatic type inference
- **Result**: No rounding, no scientific notation

#### 7.2.2 Decimal Precision
```
Input:  0.0000000000673849
Output: 0.0000000000673849
(NOT: 6.73849e-11)

Input:  123.456789012345678
Output: 123.456789012345678
(NOT: 123.45678901234568)
```

### 7.3 Performance Characteristics

#### 7.3.1 Processing Speed
| Operation | Time (approximate) |
|-----------|-------------------|
| File detection | <1 second |
| Read small file (<1MB) | 1-2 seconds |
| Read large file (10MB) | 5-10 seconds |
| Extract data | <1 second |
| Write CSV output | 1-2 seconds |
| Write Excel output | 2-5 seconds |

#### 7.3.2 Memory Usage
| File Size | RAM Required | Notes |
|-----------|--------------|-------|
| <1MB | ~50MB | Minimal overhead |
| 1-10MB | ~100-200MB | Linear scaling |
| 10-50MB | ~200-500MB | Consider optimization |
| >50MB | ~500MB+ | Monitor system resources |

#### 7.3.3 Scalability Limits
- **Max rows per sheet**: ~1 million (pandas limit)
- **Max columns**: ~16,000 (Excel limit)
- **Max file size**: 100MB recommended, 500MB maximum
- **Concurrent files**: 1 (sequential processing)

### 7.4 System Resource Requirements

#### 7.4.1 Minimum Requirements
- **CPU**: 1 core, 1 GHz
- **RAM**: 512MB
- **Disk**: 100MB for application
- **Network**: 1 Mbps (for network shares)

#### 7.4.2 Recommended Requirements
- **CPU**: 2 cores, 2 GHz
- **RAM**: 2GB
- **Disk**: 1GB for application and logs
- **Network**: 10 Mbps or higher

### 7.5 File Locking Behavior

#### 7.5.1 Input File Access
- Opens in **read-only mode**
- Does not lock file
- Safe for concurrent reading by other processes

#### 7.5.2 Output File Creation
- Atomic write operations
- Creates new file each time
- No overwrite risk (timestamp in filename)

### 7.6 Network Considerations

#### 7.6.1 Network Share Access
- Uses OS-level network authentication
- Inherits user permissions
- Subject to network latency
- Affected by SMB/CIFS protocol limitations

#### 7.6.2 Recommended Network Configuration
- Stable connection required
- Low latency preferred (<50ms)
- Sufficient bandwidth (10 Mbps minimum)
- UNC path support (Windows) or proper mounts (Linux)

