## 8. Data Processing Logic

### 8.1 File Reading Logic

#### 8.1.1 Header Handling Decision Tree
```
Read File
    │
    ├─ input_has_header = True
    │   │
    │   ├─ Pandas reads row 1 as column names
    │   ├─ Row 1 excluded from data
    │   └─ row_start=1 means first DATA row (actual row 2)
    │
    └─ input_has_header = False
        │
        ├─ Pandas treats all rows as data
        ├─ No column names assigned
        └─ row_start=1 means first FILE row
```

#### 8.1.2 Read Operation Pseudo-code
```python
IF file_extension in ['.xlsx', '.xls', '.xlsm']:
    IF input_has_header:
        dataframe = read_excel(file, header=0, dtype=str)
    ELSE:
        dataframe = read_excel(file, header=None, dtype=str)
ELIF file_extension == '.csv':
    IF input_has_header:
        dataframe = read_csv(file, header=0, dtype=str)
    ELSE:
        dataframe = read_csv(file, header=None, dtype=str)
```

### 8.2 Data Extraction Logic

#### 8.2.1 Column Selection
```python
# Input columns: ['P', 'Q', 'R']
# Converted to indices: [15, 16, 17]

extracted_df = source_df.iloc[:, [15, 16, 17]]
# Result: DataFrame with only columns P, Q, R
```

#### 8.2.2 Row Selection
```python
# Configuration: row_start=10, row_end=100

# Convert to 0-based indexing
start_idx = 10 - 1  # = 9
end_idx = 100       # = 100 (pandas slicing is exclusive at end)

extracted_df = extracted_df.iloc[9:100]
# Result: Rows 10-100 (inclusive), which is indices 9-99
```

#### 8.2.3 Complete Extraction Example
```
Original DataFrame (input_has_header=False):
     0    1    2    ...  15       16       17
0    A1   B1   C1   ...  P1       Q1       R1
1    A2   B2   C2   ...  P2       Q2       R2
...
99   A100 B100 C100 ...  P100     Q100     R100

Configuration:
    columns: ['P', 'Q', 'R']  → [15, 16, 17]
    row_start: 10
    row_end: 50

Step 1 - Select columns:
     15   16   17
0    P1   Q1   R1
1    P2   Q2   R2
...
99   P100 Q100 R100

Step 2 - Select rows 10-50 (indices 9-50):
     15   16   17
9    P10  Q10  R10
10   P11  Q11  R11
...
49   P50  Q50  R50

Result: 41 rows, 3 columns
```

