### Appendix A: Column Letter to Index Conversion

```
A = 0      N = 13     AA = 26
B = 1      O = 14     AB = 27
C = 2      P = 15     AC = 28
D = 3      Q = 16     AD = 29
E = 4      R = 17     AE = 30
F = 5      S = 18     ...
G = 6      T = 19     AZ = 51
H = 7      U = 20     BA = 52
I = 8      V = 21     ...
J = 9      W = 22     ZZ = 701
K = 10     X = 23
L = 11     Y = 24
M = 12     Z = 25
```

**Formula**:
```
For single letter: INDEX = ORD(letter) - ORD('A')
For two letters: INDEX = (first_letter × 26) + second_letter - 1
```

